---
---

<section id="about" class="min-h-screen flex items-center justify-center pt-20 px-6">
  <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto w-full">
    <div class="synth-border rounded-xl overflow-hidden glow">
      <!-- Terminal chrome -->
      <div class="flex items-center gap-2 px-4 py-3 bg-surface border-b border-surface-light/30">
        <div class="w-3 h-3 rounded-full bg-red-500/80"></div>
        <div class="w-3 h-3 rounded-full bg-yellow-500/80"></div>
        <div class="w-3 h-3 rounded-full bg-green-500/80"></div>
      </div>

      <!-- Terminal body -->
      <div class="p-8 sm:p-10 font-mono text-base sm:text-lg leading-relaxed space-y-5">
        <p class="text-text-secondary text-sm sm:text-base">
          <span class="text-neon-blue">$</span> cat about-me.txt
        </p>

        <p class="text-text-secondary text-lg sm:text-xl">
          Hello, my name is
        </p>

        <h1 class="text-4xl sm:text-5xl md:text-6xl font-bold text-text-primary synth-glow-text leading-tight">
          Unni P
        </h1>

        <p class="text-text-secondary text-base sm:text-lg">
          <span class="text-accent">I build resilient systems at scale</span>
        </p>

        <div class="h-px bg-gradient-to-r from-neon-blue/20 via-surface-light/30 to-transparent"></div>

        <p class="text-neon-blue font-semibold text-sm sm:text-base">
          Site Reliability Engineer | 8+ Years Keeping Infrastructure Standing
        </p>

        <div class="space-y-4 text-base sm:text-lg">
          <p class="text-text-secondary">
            I help engineering teams at <span class="text-neon-blue">Improving</span> ship faster without breaking production. My path started in Linux administration, moved through DevOps, and landed in SRE, so I've felt the pain at every layer of the stack, from a misconfigured cron job to a cluster-wide outage at 2am.
          </p>
          <p class="text-text-secondary">
            These days I focus on Kubernetes, cloud-native architecture, and the pipelines and guardrails that let teams move fast with confidence instead of fear.
          </p>
          <p class="text-text-secondary">
            Reliability isn't something one engineer bolts on at the end, it's a team sport. The best systems come from shared ownership, clear communication, and a culture where "how do we prevent this next time" matters as much as "how do we fix this now." Security and precision aren't afterthoughts; they're built in from the start.
          </p>
          <p class="text-text-secondary">
            When I'm not in the middle of clusters and pipelines, I'm usually deep in a new tool or writing about what I've learned, the best way to really understand something is to try explaining it to someone else.
          </p>
        </div>

        <p class="text-text-secondary text-base sm:text-lg">
          <span class="text-neon-blue">$</span> <span class="cursor-blink"></span>
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-4 mt-8 justify-center">
      <a
        href="#experience"
        class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-6 py-3 bg-accent text-primary font-semibold rounded-lg hover:bg-accent-dim transition-all duration-200 hover:shadow-[0_0_25px_rgba(255,42,109,0.4)]"
      >
        View My Experience
        <svg class="w-4 h-4" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
          <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M17 8l4 4m0 0l-4 4m4-4H3" />
        </svg>
      </a>
      <a
        href="#projects"
        class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-6 py-3 border border-neon-blue/40 text-neon-blue font-semibold rounded-lg hover:border-neon-blue hover:shadow-[0_0_20px_rgba(5,217,232,0.2)] transition-all duration-200"
      >
        View My Work
      </a>
      <a
        href="#contact"
        class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-6 py-3 border border-neon-blue/40 text-neon-blue font-semibold rounded-lg hover:border-neon-blue hover:shadow-[0_0_20px_rgba(5,217,232,0.2)] transition-all duration-200"
      >
        Get In Touch
      </a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
